        "title": "06 - Thematic Maps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A reference map says \"here is where things are.\" A thematic map says \"here is what varies where.\" The distinction is fundamental. Thematic maps are rhetorical devices — arguments encoded in spatial form. Every choice of map type, color scheme, data classification, and projection is an argument about what the data means."
    },
