        "section": "cartography",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "06 - Thematic Maps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The 1854 Broad Street cholera outbreak in Soho, London, is the most cited case study in the history of spatial analysis. Snow's map is typically described as the founding document of epidemiology. The actual story is more nuanced and more interesting."
    },
