        "title": "06 - Thematic Maps",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BACKGROUND:\n  - August 31, 1854: cholera cases begin appearing in Soho\n  - Within 10 days: 500 deaths in a small geographic area\n  - Prevailing theory: miasma (disease caused by bad air)\n  - Snow's theory (since 1849): cholera spread by contaminated water"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-THEMATIC-MAPS.md#014",
      "path": [
        "06-THEMATIC-MAPS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
